Patch X1 (rung 1b, gate G5): xtask sets the version stamp's source-tree values.

Every cargo command that xtask runs gets ENG_ENGINE_SHA, ENG_DIRTY,
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH and ENG_CI_RUN, worked out once per run from git and
GitHub Actions' variables; a non-empty value already set wins. A build
made through xtask then has no `unknown` in its stamp. Amendments 15 and
16 of docs/rungs/1b/PROGRESS.md describe it; the session entry that
added this file says how it was tested.

Base: main at 106a8f0. Apply at the repo root with `git apply`, then run
`cargo xtask quick`, `cargo xtask selftest` and `cargo test -p xtask`.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

